 "caution": "18.2 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 131,074 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages. Maithili (Devanagari) is an abugida: CV (orthographic) counts every consonant letter as C plus an inherent vowel V unless a vowel sign or virama follows. CV (phonological) applies the Hindi-type schwa-deletion rule (not checked against pronunciations). Length is counted in aksharas.",
